From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 01:12:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] encode: offer packed sequence headers so clients can write
 extradata

The stateful encoder writes SPS/PPS (and the HEVC VPS) in band in front of
every IDR, so the driver reported no packed header support. FFmpeg's VA-API
encoders only build extradata (avcC / hvcC) when the driver offers
VA_ENC_PACKED_HEADER_SEQUENCE. With a container that needs the parameter
sets in its header, Matroska in particular, the muxer then rejects the empty
CodecPrivate (ff_isom_write_avcc, AVERROR_INVALIDDATA) before the first frame
is sent, and FFmpeg 9.0.2 crashes on the end-of-stream path of its encoder
(hw_base_encode.c:508, NULL pic_end).

Offer VA_ENC_PACKED_HEADER_SEQUENCE. The packed header buffers a client then
submits are already accepted and dropped by the render path, so the
bitstream still carries the encoder's own parameter sets; the client's copy
only goes into the container header.
---
 src/encode.c | 11 +++++++++--
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/encode.c b/src/encode.c
index 3af03fa..4c6f56f 100644
--- a/src/encode.c
+++ b/src/encode.c
@@ -159,8 +159,15 @@ uint32_t v4l2r_encoder_attribute(VAProfile profile, VAConfigAttribType type)
 	case VAConfigAttribRateControl:
 		return VA_RC_CQP | VA_RC_CBR | VA_RC_VBR;
 	case VAConfigAttribEncPackedHeaders:
-		/* The encoder writes its own parameter sets in band. */
-		return VA_ENC_PACKED_HEADER_NONE;
+		/*
+		 * The encoder writes its own parameter sets in band, in front of
+		 * every IDR. Offering packed sequence headers anyway lets a client
+		 * build them for its container (FFmpeg writes extradata, i.e. avcC /
+		 * hvcC, only with this bit); the packed buffers it then sends are
+		 * accepted and dropped in v4l2r_enc_render. Without it, Matroska
+		 * refuses the stream before the first frame (empty CodecPrivate).
+		 */
+		return VA_ENC_PACKED_HEADER_SEQUENCE;
 	case VAConfigAttribEncMaxRefFrames:
 		/* One forward reference, no backward: no B-frames. */
 		return 1;
-- 
2.43.0

